    "publishedDate": "2026-03-03",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Hello Guest,\n\nThank you for taking the time to share your feedback following your recent stay with us.\n\nI am very sorry to read that your experience was disappointing overall. Please accept my sincere apologies for the condition of the apartment upon arrival. The cleanliness concerns you described should never have occurred, and while I appreciate that our team attended to the room promptly, this should certainly not have been necessary immediately after check-in.\n\nI also apologize for the inconsistent and unclear communication regarding housekeeping services. We recognize that this lack of clarity and follow-through impacted your stay, and we are reviewing our processes to ensure service expectations are clearly communicated and consistently delivered.\n\nYour feedback regarding the disclosure of pet fees is equally important. Transparency around additional charges is essential so guests can make informed decisions and budget accordingly.\n\nWhile I am pleased to hear that our receptionist was able to assist by providing extension leads for your CPAP machines, I acknowledge that the lack of accessible power outlets by the bedside is an inconvenience. Your comments have been shared with our concerned team as we assess improvements in this area.\n\nWe genuinely regret that we did not meet expectations on this occasion. Your feedback is valued and will assist us in improving our communication, cleaning standards, and overall guest experience. Should you be open to it, I would welcome the opportunity to speak with you directly to further discuss your stay.\n\nKind regards,\n\nAmit\nGeneral Manager\nQuest Macquarie Park",
    "username": "Quest Macquarie Park",
    "connectionToSubject": "Guest Services / Front Office",
